;; =======================================================
;; FUNDAMENTAL MODE -- OVERVIEW
;; =======================================================
;;
;; |------------------+-------------------+---------------------------------|
;; | OVERVIEW         | TRIGGER           |                                 |
;; |------------------+-------------------+---------------------------------|
;; | Emacs            | <em               | General Emacs questions         |
;; | Trading          | <tr               | General Trading questions       |
;; | Linux            | <lx               | General Linux questions         |
;; | BASH/ZSH         | <sh               | General BASH/ZSH questions      |
;; | Python           | <py               | General Python questions        |
;; | Window Managers  | <wm               | General WM's questions          |
;; | Academics        | <uni              | General Academics questions     |
;; |------------------+-------------------+---------------------------------|
;; | GEN. CONSTRAINTS | <rule-gen         | For ALL variations              |
;; |------------------+-------------------+---------------------------------|
;; |                  | <rule-gen-80      | Strict 80-char column limit     |
;; |                  | <rule-gen-roam    | Output as .org for org-roam     |
;; |                  | <rule-gen-10yo    | Explain for a 10-year-old       |
;; |                  | <rule-gen-nofluff | Skip greetings, go to solution  |
;; |                  | <rule-gen-fact    | No guessing, state uncertainty  |
;; |                  | <rule-gen-short   | Short/Concise Clear Explanation |
;; |------------------+-------------------+---------------------------------|
;; | SPF. CONSTRAINTS | <rule-[..]        | Tailored to SPECIFICS           |
;; |------------------+-------------------+---------------------------------|

(<rule-80
"%+80 char column RULE+%" n
 "Format the text to strictly fit an 80-character column limit. "
 "Keep it short, concise, and technical, but simple to understand." n q)

(<rule-roam
"%+Output answer as .org Emacs file+%" n
 "Output the final answer as an .org file for org-roam archival." n q)

(<rule-10yo
"%+Explain for a 10y old+%" n
 "Explain the concepts so clearly that a 10-year-old would "
 "easily understand them." n q)

(<rule-nofluff
"%+No greetings and ego massage+%" n
 "Cut the greetings and ego massage, jump to the solutions right away." n q)

(<rule-fact
"%+Anti-Hallucination RULE+%" n
 "If you do not know the exact answer "
 "or the data is ambiguous, state 'I do not have enough verifiable "
 "information' instead of guessing." n q)

(<rule-gen-short
"%+Short/Concise Clear Explanation+%" n
"As a technical writer who distills complex topics into short, "
"dense explanations. Every sentence must carry weight. Cut filler, "
"keep precision. Prefer concrete examples over abstract descriptions. "
"keep it short and concise, so explain the last answer accordingly"
n q)

(<rule-gen-link_text
"%+Summarize Chat Shortly Give Links+%" n
"This conversation has been really useful and I would like to implement the majority (if not all) of your suggestions for this I would need you to do a short/concise summary of our discussed topic along with links for me to jump straight to every answer, because having to screen scrolling sucks.. I would need the points about: " n
(p "- (copy/paste answer to summarize and link)") n
(p "- (copy/paste answer to summarize and link)") n q)


